></mxCell><mxCell id="r5c3" value="YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="595" y="420" width="285" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="r5c4" value="W06-S02" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="880" y="420" width="249" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="r6c0" value="photo_ref" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="468" width="145" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="r6c1" value="Attachment reference for the image; no image files supplied" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="185" y="468" width="220" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="r6c2" value="IMG-603" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="405" y="468" width="190" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="r6c3" value="IMG- followed by three digits" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="595" y="468" width="285" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="r6c4" value="W06-S02" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="880" y="468" width="249" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="r7c0" value="survey_area" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="516" width="145" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="r7c1" value="Fictional survey area of the city; not a coordinate" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="185" y="516" width="220" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="r7c2" value="CENTRAL" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="405" y="516" width="190" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="r7c3" value="NORTH, CENTRAL or SOUTH" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="595" y="516" width="285" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="r7c4" value="W06-S02" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="880" y="516" width="249" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="finding" value="&lt;b&gt;Finding.&lt;/b&gt; Report &lt;b&gt;CJ-603&lt;/b&gt; (asset_type BRIDGE, survey_area CENTRAL, ROUTINE) had an expected destination of &lt;b&gt;Structures&lt;/b&gt; and an observed destination of &lt;b&gt;Electrical&lt;/b&gt;. Fields from W06-S02; required destination from W06-S03; observed destination from the delivery log in W06-S04; process path from W06-S01. The same mismatch appears for CJ-604 and CJ-607, the other two BRIDGE reports, so no BRIDGE report in this export reached Structures, while every STREETLIGHT and DRAIN report reached its required department. Priority is not the factor: those three are one URGENT and two ROUTINE, and W06-S03 states that urgency does not change the department. All eight reports were ACCEPTED, so the eight required fields were present and the discrepancy arises after P2 Check Required Fields. This is an observed result, not an established cause.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Unanswered question.&lt;/b&gt; What routing entries did D2 Routing Table hold when these work items were sent? W06-S03 gives the required mapping but states it does not prove what the running table contained, and no runtime snapshot, deployment history or code was supplied. A dated export of D2 and its change history, which a service administrator maintains outside this boundary, would be needed to establish the cause. [W06-S01, W06-S03, W06-S04]" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontColor=#18333e;strokeColor=#4d7682;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="585" width="1089" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>